{"ts":"2026-08-28T15:09:32.562Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-5.6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"143da6b99c6d50ff73f411da","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-5.6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gactwj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Broad squash commits overflow hosted-analysis tree lookup and falsely lose reviewed PR provenance"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The hosted analysis gate reads each commit through the heavyweight REST commits endpoint using spawnSync with Node default buffering. PR #1133 merged a 105-file squash whose response exceeds that buffer, so the subprocess terminates with status null and the gate treats the merge tree as unavailable even though GitHub associates PR #1133 and the merge/head trees are identical."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":0},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["analyzer-provenance","area:ci","area:release","defect-escape","github-actions","regression"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-28T15:09:32.562Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-28T15:09:32.562Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The gate requests commit tree metadata from a narrow immutable endpoint whose payload does not scale with changed-file patches; A focused negative regression proves the old heavyweight lookup would overflow while the new lookup resolves the exact tree; Fail-closed behavior for missing or malformed tree metadata remains intact; Focused tests, exact 100/100/100/100 repository coverage, static quality, manual temporary-directory acceptance, exact-head PR review, merged-main analyzer readiness, and release gates pass"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/definition_of_ready","value":"Production failure, exact merge/head/tree evidence, buffer root cause, canonical lineage, and no-duplicate all-status search are recorded."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make reviewed-PR analyzer provenance deterministic for arbitrarily broad squash commits without increasing unbounded subprocess buffering."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Broad SDK and CLI deliveries can pass the mandatory merged-main analyzer readiness gate and proceed to immutable release without weakening provenance."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"The only failed job on merged-main CI run 33182695715 blocks the 2026.8.28 release despite every product, coverage, static, compatibility, smoke, and Windows job passing."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Commit tree lookup uses a bounded Git database endpoint, retains fail-closed behavior, and has a regression test that prevents large standard commit payloads from reintroducing false provenance loss."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"PR #1133 is merged and release-ready except for this production defect; release must remain blocked until a reviewed fix passes exact-main CI."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"GitHub Actions hosted runner; unbraind/pm-cli main merge 0480ab6668d2699acc63558acf99c02bd3b5a571; CI run 33182695715 job 98887669749; Node spawnSync; GitHub REST API"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Run scripts/release/hosted-analysis-gate.mjs for merge 0480ab6668d2699acc63558acf99c02bd3b5a571. The PR association resolves to #1133 and head 9f56a49524ae14d34e4a7c39370739bf2c4e2e9e; both git trees are 54f43f0400fcf0af653053cad1253cec7ca0ace1, but repos/unbraind/pm-cli/commits/<merge> exceeds spawnSync default maxBuffer and readCommitTree returns null."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A reviewed squash merge with an identical reviewed head tree satisfies analyzer provenance regardless of the number of changed files."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The standard commits endpoint emits more than one MiB of file and patch data; spawnSync returns status null, readCommitTree returns null, and the gate reports no exact or identical-tree reviewed evidence."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.8.28"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"release automation / hosted analysis provenance"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/regression","value":true},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"No broken artifact was published, but the valid daily SDK/CLI release is blocked until provenance lookup is repaired."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-8pnj","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-28T15:09:32.562Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-e70zh5","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-28T15:09:32.562Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-u1baah","kind":"recurs_from","created_at":"2026-08-28T15:09:32.562Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-28T15:09:32.562Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate-check and production evidence 2026-08-28: inspected all-status searches for the exact title, ENOBUFS, maxBuffer, and hosted-analysis commit-tree provenance; no item owns this broad-squash failure. Canonical pm-u1baah is closed with shipped analyzer-provenance behavior, so this item records a recurrence instead of reopening or duplicating that completed work. GitHub associates merge 0480ab6668d2699acc63558acf99c02bd3b5a571 with PR #1133 head 9f56a49524ae14d34e4a7c39370739bf2c4e2e9e, both trees equal 54f43f0400fcf0af653053cad1253cec7ca0ace1, and instrumentation shows the heavyweight commit request exits with null status after exceeding the default spawnSync buffer."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"8cf670d850c41453646100df009f740fb16b9e20bde48b1cd17700dbf43faebf","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Record broad-squash analyzer provenance buffer regression","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
